# Where the Workers API lives.
#
# PUBLIC_ is required: Astro only exposes variables with that prefix to client
# code, and every call from /admin and /resultados is made from the browser.
# Inlined at build time, so a deploy needs this set before `astro build`, not
# at runtime.
#
# Three cases, and the difference between the last two is easy to get wrong:
#
#   unset   -> falls back to http://localhost:8787, the wrangler dev port. This
#              is local development with two servers (Astro on :4321, wrangler
#              on :8787), so `pnpm dev` works with no .env file at all.
#
#   empty   -> same origin, relative URLs. This is PRODUCTION: one Worker serves
#              both the built frontend and the API, so there is no other host to
#              point at. `pnpm build` from the repo root sets it empty for
#              exactly this reason.
#
#   a URL   -> that host. Only needed if the API is ever deployed somewhere the
#              frontend is not, which the current topology avoids.
#
# scripts/admin/api.js reads it with `??`, not `||`, so an empty value survives
# instead of being mistaken for unset and sent to localhost in a production build.
PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://localhost:8787
